Repair creates another material state (@mat-material-repair: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #materials-engineering "../../mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/service/Repair-restoration-and-return-to-service.lingua#r_1RF5PD4EHJKFZ57X6RSFKXJK1X") { r_7ZXVYZHCAXBQG85W3HK11CZBC8
**Read:** The shared mechanical restoration Record; the complete joining, coating, heat-treatment and interface references relevant to the chosen material.

Welding, bonding, deposition, machining and local heat can restore geometry while changing composition, residual stress, texture, flaw populations or nearby interfaces. A repaired state is neither automatically new nor automatically unusable. Its remaining function depends on the actual transformation and evidence.

Retain the history of removed material, added feed, heat input, surface preparation and inspection. Distinguish restoring dimensions from restoring load transfer, sealing, conductivity or optical function. A treatment that improves one mechanism can worsen another or make future inspection harder.

**Work:** Compare repair and replacement for one documented component. Derive the local thermal/mechanical or chemical effects of the repair and identify the region requiring characterization. Define what evidence supports a return to the stated function and what uncertainty remains. Compare subsequent service and recovery implications rather than judging only the immediate material saved.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
